---
import TabTabScreenshot from "../../components/TabTabScreenshot.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "TabTab vs AltTab: Windows and Tabs in One Search";
const description = "Compare TabTab's window-and-tab search with AltTab's visual window switching for Mac.";
const siteUrl = Astro.site ?? new URL("https://tabtabapp.net");
const pageUrl = new URL("/compare/alttab/", siteUrl).href;
const imageUrl = new URL("/og-image.png", siteUrl).href;
const structuredData = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  headline: title,
  description,
  image: imageUrl,
  datePublished: "2026-08-15",
  dateModified: "2026-09-06",
  mainEntityOfPage: pageUrl,
  author: {
    "@type": "Person",
    name: "Richard Qi",
  },
  publisher: {
    "@type": "Organization",
    name: "TabTab",
    url: new URL("/", siteUrl).href,
  },
  about: [
    { "@type": "SoftwareApplication", name: "TabTab", operatingSystem: "macOS" },
    { "@type": "SoftwareApplication", name: "AltTab", operatingSystem: "macOS" },
  ],
};

const comparisonRows = [
  ["Searches", "Windows and individual tabs", "Windows only"],
  ["Tab workflow", "Search once and open the tab", "Switch windows, then find the tab inside the app"],
  ["Tab URL search", "Yes", "No"],
  ["Interface", "Clean, compact UI with app icons, browser favicons, and mouse support", "Window previews, app icon, and title layouts"],
  ["Keyboard shortcuts", "Familiar macOS defaults and multiple custom shortcuts", "Extensive shortcut customisation"],
  ["Switcher actions", "Minimize windows; close windows and tabs", "Close, minimize, and fullscreen windows"],
  ["Privacy", "No personal data stored; limited anonymous analytics", "Usage statistics stay local"],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  socialImage="/og-image.png"
  ogType="article"
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <article class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-8 py-20 md:px-12 md:py-28">
      <header class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h1 class="text-5xl font-medium leading-[1.04] tracking-tight text-black font-display md:text-6xl">
          TabTab vs AltTab: 2026 comparison
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600">
          Find the window or tab you need with one search. TabTab searches across windows and individual tabs in supported apps, so you can jump straight back to your work.
        </p>
      </header>

      <figure class="mx-auto mt-16 max-w-3xl">
        <TabTabScreenshot
          alt="TabTab search interface listing windows and tabs from Safari, Chrome, Arc, VS Code, Cursor, Figma, and other Mac apps"
          class="h-auto w-full rounded-2xl"
        />
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-center text-sm text-gray-500">
          TabTab: Search app names, window titles, tab titles, and URLs.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <section class="mx-auto mt-16 max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-black font-display md:text-4xl">Go straight to the tab you need</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600">
          <p>
            Both switch windows. TabTab also keeps track of visible, minimized, and hidden windows. It searches tabs by title or URL. AltTab leaves tab search to the app after you switch.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            A single browser or code editor window can hold many tabs. TabTab can match a website, document, repository, or part of a URL that you remember. It opens the result directly in supported apps such as Safari, Chrome, Arc, Firefox, VS Code, Cursor, Finder, and Figma.
          </p>
          <dl class="mt-7 grid gap-3 text-lg text-gray-700">
            <div class="grid grid-cols-[7rem_1fr] gap-4"><dt class="font-semibold text-accent-600">TabTab</dt><dd>Find window or tab → switch</dd></div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-[7rem_1fr] gap-4"><dt class="font-semibold text-black">AltTab</dt><dd>Find window → switch → find the tab inside the app</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <h3 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-black">Example: finding an open GitHub issue</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Suppose an issue is open in one of several browser windows. With TabTab, search for a distinctive word in the issue title or part of its URL, then select the tracked tab. With AltTab, choose the browser window first, then use the browser's tab search to locate the issue.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you remember a window's appearance instead of its title, AltTab's thumbnails may make it easier to recognize. For the search workflow, follow the <a class="text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700" href="/guides/search-open-tabs-on-mac/">guide to searching open tabs on Mac</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mx-auto mt-20 max-w-5xl">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-black font-display md:text-4xl">At a glance</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-gray-200">
          <table class="w-full min-w-[760px] border-collapse text-left text-sm md:text-base">
            <thead class="border-b border-gray-300 text-black">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-5 py-4 font-semibold">Feature</th>
                <th class="bg-sky-50 px-5 py-4 font-semibold text-accent-700">TabTab</th>
                <th class="px-5 py-4 font-semibold">AltTab</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200">
              {comparisonRows.map(([feature, tabtab, alttab]) => (
                <tr class="align-top">
                  <th class="px-5 py-4 font-semibold text-black">{feature}</th>
                  <td class="bg-sky-50 px-5 py-4 font-medium text-gray-800">{tabtab}</td>
                  <td class="px-5 py-4 text-gray-600">{alttab}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="mx-auto mt-14 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-black font-display md:text-4xl">Find your place at a glance</h2>
          <p class="mt-5">
            App icons, browser favicons, titles, and URLs help you recognize the right result in a compact list.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            AltTab includes thumbnail, app icon, and title layouts.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Use the keyboard or mouse to choose a TabTab result. Optional mouse activation opens TabTab when you move the cursor to the screen edge.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mx-auto mt-14 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-black font-display md:text-4xl">Familiar shortcuts. Now for your tabs, too.</h2>
          <p class="mt-5">
            TabTab mirrors familiar macOS app-switcher shortcuts wherever possible, so it feels natural from the first use. It also supports multiple custom keyboard shortcuts, including one that opens search directly. Inside the switcher, familiar keyboard commands can minimize a window or close the selected window or tab without making you switch to it first.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            AltTab offers extensive shortcut customisation and several window controls. TabTab keeps the setup straightforward and brings the same quick workflow to windows and individual tabs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mx-auto mt-16 max-w-4xl rounded-2xl bg-gray-950 p-8 text-center text-white md:p-10">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight font-display md:text-4xl">One search for every window and tab</h2>
            <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-gray-300">Your next task is already open somewhere. Find it with TabTab.</p>
          </div>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/riccqi/TabTabApp/releases/download/prod/tabtab-latest.dmg"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="mt-7 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-white px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-black transition hover:bg-sky-100"
          >Download TabTab</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <p class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-4xl text-sm leading-6 text-gray-400">
        Updated 2026. Sources: <a class="underline hover:text-black" href="/pricing/">TabTab pricing</a>, <a class="underline hover:text-black" href="/privacy/">TabTab privacy</a>, <a class="underline hover:text-black" href="https://alt-tab.app/vs/tabtab" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AltTab comparison</a>, <a class="underline hover:text-black" href="https://alt-tab.app/features" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AltTab features</a>, and <a class="underline hover:text-black" href="https://alt-tab.app/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AltTab privacy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
